# GSP355: Create and Manage Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL Instances - Challenge Lab Guide

## Environment Variables Setup
Run this block in **Cloud Shell** before executing tasks. Ensure you replace the placeholder values with the exact credentials from your Qwiklabs details pane.

```bash
# Set your lab variables
export REGION="<YOUR_LAB_REGION>"             # e.g., us-central1
export ZONE="<YOUR_LAB_ZONE>"                 # e.g., us-central1-a
export PROJECT_ID=$(gcloud config get-value project)
export DB_NAME="orders"
export MIGRATION_JOB="orders-migration"
export CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE="<YOUR_MIGRATED_INSTANCE_ID>" # from lab instructions (e.g., postgres-orders)
export DB_USER="<YOUR_QWIKLABS_USERNAME>"    # e.g., student-xx@qwiklabs.net

# Set defaults to avoid empty parameter errors
gcloud config set compute/region $REGION
gcloud config set compute/zone $ZONE
Task 1: Migrate Standalone PostgreSQL to Cloud SQL
1. Configure the Source Database VM
SSH into postgres-vm from Cloud Shell or the Cloud Console:

Bash
gcloud compute ssh postgres-vm --zone=$ZONE
Inside postgres-vm, configure PostgreSQL for logical replication and add the missing primary key:

Bash
# Switch to postgres user and connect to the orders database
sudo -u postgres psql -d orders -c "ALTER TABLE distribution_centers ADD PRIMARY KEY (id);"

# Ensure the pglogical extension is active
sudo -u postgres psql -d orders -c "CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pglogical;"

# Exit the VM
exit
2. Create DMS Connection Profile & Start Migration Job
Run in Cloud Shell:

Bash
# Get the internal IP of postgres-vm
VM_INTERNAL_IP=$(gcloud compute instances describe postgres-vm --zone=$ZONE --format='get(networkInterfaces[0].networkIP)')

# Create Connection Profile for the source VM
gcloud database-migration connection-profiles create postgresql postgres-vm-profile \
    --region=$REGION \
    --host=$VM_INTERNAL_IP \
    --port=5432 \
    --username=postgres \
    --password="supersecret!" \
    --provider=POSTGRESQL

# Create and run the continuous migration job
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs create $MIGRATION_JOB \
    --region=$REGION \
    --source=postgres-vm-profile \
    --destination-instance-id=$CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --type=CONTINUOUS \
    --connectivity-vpc=default

# Start the job
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs start $MIGRATION_JOB --region=$REGION
Task 2: Promote Cloud SQL to Stand-Alone Instance
1. Monitor Migration Progress (Fixed Watch Command)
Note: We dynamically detect $REGION so the --region argument is never empty.

Bash
# Check migration job status until PHASE shows CDC / RUNNING
watch -n 5 "gcloud database-migration migration-jobs describe $MIGRATION_JOB --region=\$(gcloud config get-value compute/region) --format='table(state,phase)'"
(Press Ctrl + C once the status transitions to RUNNING or change data capture).

2. Promote the Cloud SQL Instance
Promote via gcloud CLI (or select Promote inside Database Migration > Migration Jobs in the Console):

Bash
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs promote $MIGRATION_JOB \
    --region=$REGION \
    --quiet
Wait 2–3 minutes for the instance to detach and finish restarting as a standalone instance.

Task 3: Secure the Database Using IAM DB Authentication
Enable IAM DB Authentication flag:

Bash
gcloud sql instances patch $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --database-flags=cloudsql.iam_authentication=on
Authorize the postgres-vm external IP on Cloud SQL:

Bash
VM_EXT_IP=$(gcloud compute instances describe postgres-vm --zone=$ZONE --format='get(networkInterfaces[0].accessConfigs[0].natIP)')

gcloud sql instances patch $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --authorized-networks=$VM_EXT_IP
Add Cloud IAM user:

Bash
gcloud sql users create $DB_USER \
    --instance=$CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --type=CLOUD_IAM_USER
Grant SELECT permissions inside the database:

Bash
gcloud sql connect $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE --user=postgres --quiet
(When prompted for password, enter supersecret!)

SQL
\c orders;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA public TO "$DB_USER";
\q
Task 4: Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR)
Enable Point-in-Time Recovery and automated backups:

Bash
gcloud sql instances patch $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --enable-point-in-time-recovery \
    --enable-bin-log
Verify clone creation if specified in lab requirements (postgres-orders-pitr):

Bash
gcloud sql instances clone $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE${CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE}-pitr
